witzerland and Italy, with Annecy as its prefecture.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hautes-pyrenees"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/hautes-pyrenees.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hautes-Pyrénées</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hautes-Pyrénées is a department in south-western France on the Spanish border, in the Occitanie region, with Tarbes as its prefecture.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/havana"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/havana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Havana</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Havana is the capital and largest city of Cuba, founded by the Spanish in 1515 and moved to its present site on a sheltered bay around 1519.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/havel"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/havel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Havel</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Havel is a river in north-eastern Germany, about 330 kilometres long, a right tributary of the Elbe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/havelberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/havelberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Havelberg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Havelberg is a small town on the Havel near its junction with the Elbe in Saxony-Anhalt, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/haveli"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/haveli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Haveli</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">A haveli is a traditional townhouse or mansion of the Indian 